---
description: Persistent AI team coordination rules for this repository
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` and `collaboration/AI_TEAM_PROTOCOL.md` before material work.

Operate as part of a two-agent GitHub workflow:
- Cursor is Lead Engineering Agent.
- ChatGPT/JARVIS is Systems Architect / Chief of Staff.
- Human owner retains final authority over strategic and irreversible actions.

Canonical branch: `main`.
Working lanes: `agent/cursor`, `agent/chatgpt`.
Substantial isolated work: `work/<agent>/<task-id>-<slug>`.

Never silently overwrite another agent's material changes.
Do not push directly to `main` unless the repository owner explicitly requests a controlled bootstrap/admin action.
Use Issues for agent handoffs and PRs for integration/review.
After material work: commit, push, record verification, then sync from `main` after merges.

Repository-specific instructions and disclosure/security rules take precedence over generic workflow details.
